444637,0.012048653326928616,0.02272745408117771,0.00104290503077209,0.030286140739917755,-0.00014591659419238567,0.002718221629038453,-0.007307023275643587,0.011520610190927982,0.001769658294506371,-0.006796372588723898,-0.01892373152077198,-0.025477256625890732,0.014410753734409809,-0.01938263140618801,0.011280884966254234,-0.014163266867399216,0.000908193935174495,0.018930798396468163,0.02933206595480442,-0.022043166682124138,Task Automation via Tools,"LLMs are fundamentally language processors and lack the inherent capability to execute external actions independently, such as reserving conference rooms or booking flight tickets.",Users requiring LLMs to perform real-world actions or automate repetitive tasks that involve interacting with external systems.,"Integrate LLMs with external task automation tools, scheduling tools, project management tools, online shopping assistants, or data table processing tools by populating their interfaces with the necessary parameters.","LLMs can facilitate the execution of external actions, automate repetitive tasks (e.g., scheduling, setting reminders, filtering emails), and enhance practical user assistance, efficiency, and user experience.","Scheduling appointments, setting reminders, filtering emails, managing project tasks, assisting with online shopping, performing data analysis and visualization.","This AI pattern, ""Task Automation via Tools,"" addresses the inherent limitation of Large Language Models (LLMs) in directly executing external actions like scheduling or booking, despite user demand for such real-world capabilities. It solves this by integrating LLMs with various external task automation, scheduling, or project management tools, where the LLM populates the necessary parameters to invoke these tools. The result is that LLMs can facilitate real-world actions, automate repetitive tasks like scheduling appointments or filtering emails, and significantly enhance practical user assistance and overall efficiency."
