010281526483595371,0.019769540056586266,0.019307631999254227,0.010450275614857674,-0.010236557573080063,-0.0027722860686481,0.008323282934725285,0.011139933951199055,-0.0041267345659434795,0.004140560515224934,0.001883690245449543,-0.002487788675352931,-0.02313387393951416,0.005760664120316505,-0.018489625304937363,0.021561384201049805,0.008141771890223026,0.023600922897458076,0.026371829211711884,0.03195222094655037,-0.018706535920500755,DivExplorer Interactive System (Interactive Divergent Subgroup Exploration),"Users need an interactive way to explore, analyze, and understand divergent model behaviors in data subgroups, particularly for identifying bias or debugging.","Structured data, black-box classification models, need for interactive exploration of divergent subgroups identified by the DivExplorer algorithm.","Integrates the DivExplorer algorithm into a web application. Provides a UI with a sortable table of divergent itemsets (with pruning), bar graphs for local item contributions (Shapley values), a lattice visualization for exploring subset relationships and corrective items, global item influence visualizations, and search/drilldown functionalities.","Facilitates interactive exploration and analysis of divergent subgroups, helping users identify bias, debug models, and understand classifier behavior at a granular level.","Analyzing and debugging classifiers, identifying bias in classifiers, exploring model behavior in data subgroups, model validation.","The DivExplorer Interactive System offers an interactive web-based platform for users to explore and understand divergent behaviors of black-box classification models within specific data subgroups. It integrates the DivExplorer algorithm with a rich user interface featuring sortable tables of divergent itemsets, local and global item contribution visualizations, and a lattice view for subset relationships. This system facilitates the identification of model bias, aids in debugging, and offers granular insights into classifier behavior for improved model validation."
