6,-0.008763889782130718,0.017036760225892067,0.010825559496879578,-0.011819961480796337,-0.004484629258513451,-0.014542125165462494,0.0026673353277146816,0.0016952317673712969,0.0001736363919917494,-0.00013399909948930144,-0.012782715260982513,-0.01317212451249361,-0.027286887168884277,0.005091862287372351,-0.025702305138111115,-0.005252965725958347,-0.004780302289873362,0.012379265390336514,0.03174077346920967,0.022915538400411606,-0.029185276478528976,Counterfactual Explanations,"Users want to understand the minimal changes to an instance's features that would alter its prediction to a desired outcome, providing actionable insights into how to achieve a specific model decision or avoid an undesired one.","Model-agnostic local interpretability for black-box classification or regression models, particularly in high-stakes decision-making or fairness analysis, where users need to know 'what if' scenarios for individual predictions.","Identify the smallest possible modifications to the feature values of a given instance that would cause the black-box model to produce a different, desired prediction outcome. This involves searching for an instance close to the original but on the other side of the decision boundary.","A modified instance (the counterfactual) that is very similar to the original but receives a different prediction, along with the specific, minimal feature changes required to achieve that outcome. This provides an intuitive and actionable explanation.","Understanding decision boundaries, providing actionable advice to users, debugging model biases, fairness analysis, building user trust by showing control over outcomes, satisfying 'right to explanation' requirements.","Counterfactual Explanations provide actionable insights by showing users the minimal changes to an instance's features that would alter a black-box model's prediction to a desired outcome. This is achieved by identifying the smallest possible modifications to an instance's feature values that cause the model to produce a different, specific prediction, effectively finding an instance just across the decision boundary. The result is an intuitive explanation detailing the precise, minimal feature adjustments required to achieve a different model decision, enhancing understanding and trust."
