7,0.021570030599832535,0.0242824237793684,-0.009243343025445938,0.010840052738785744,0.0029026633128523827,0.009263952262699604,-0.007666012737900019,0.018184801563620567,0.00020570098422467709,-0.011798708699643612,-0.004818572662770748,-0.02778511680662632,0.009790517389774323,-0.01708695851266384,-0.0038606123998761177,0.0019735312089323997,0.002683844417333603,0.013553323224186897,0.030523549765348434,-0.016705848276615143,Meta Tool Learning,"Models need to adapt their behaviors and tool-use strategies when faced with unfamiliar tools or new domains, rather than just learning to use a specific tool.","Scenarios requiring high adaptability and generalization, where an AI system needs to transfer tool-use knowledge and strategies from one tool or domain to another (e.g., from one search engine to another, or a calculator for different math problems).",Train the model not only to use a tool but also to learn the optimal *strategy* for its use. This involves identifying common underlying principles or patterns in tool-use strategies and transferring them to new tasks or domains. This is about learning *how to learn* tool use.,"Enhanced adaptability and intelligence in ML models, enabling them to generalize tool use to different types of problems or new tools, even if initially trained on specific instances.","Transferring search engine usage skills, generalizing calculator use for various mathematical problems, adapting to new software interfaces.","Meta Tool Learning addresses the challenge of enabling AI models to adapt their tool-use strategies to unfamiliar tools or new domains, rather than just mastering a single tool. The solution involves training models to learn the optimal *strategy* for tool use, identifying common underlying principles that can be transferred across different tools and tasks. This approach enhances adaptability and intelligence, allowing models to generalize tool usage, such as transferring search engine skills or adapting to new software interfaces."
