977,0.02063833549618721,0.01592935621738434,-0.0066528357565402985,0.020458057522773743,-0.010397794656455517,0.00913089420646429,-0.0016152996104210615,0.00761551083996892,0.00461253197863698,0.007326378487050533,-0.03256477043032646,-0.023905733600258827,0.006992281414568424,-0.01970379799604416,0.007804017513990402,-0.008741739206016064,0.0010476717725396156,0.013012991286814213,0.034039128571748734,-0.02871430292725563,Open-Book Question Answering with InContext RALM,"Enabling frozen, pre-trained Language Models to answer open-domain questions accurately by leveraging external knowledge, without requiring fine-tuning or specific pre-training for QA.","A large, pre-trained LM (e.g., LLaMA) is available, but it lacks the specific knowledge or reasoning capabilities to answer open-domain questions reliably in a 'closed-book' setting. Fine-tuning is not desired or possible.","Extend the standard question-answering prompt by prepending relevant documents retrieved from a knowledge source (e.g., Wikipedia via DPR) to the LM's input. The LM then processes this augmented prompt (documents + question) to generate the answer. The number of documents can be optimized.","Significantly boosted performance in open-domain question answering tasks (e.g., exact match scores on NQ and TriviaQA) for frozen LMs, demonstrating their ability to leverage retrieved documents without further training.","Building robust open-domain question answering systems, improving factual accuracy in QA, leveraging general-purpose LMs for knowledge-intensive tasks.","This pattern, ""Open-Book Question Answering with InContext RALM,"" enables frozen Language Models to accurately answer open-domain questions without fine-tuning. It works by prepending relevant external documents, retrieved from a knowledge source, directly to the LM's input prompt alongside the question. This allows the LM to leverage the provided context to generate accurate answers, significantly boosting performance on knowledge-intensive QA tasks."
