-0.008779366500675678,0.016222145408391953,0.009031414054334164,-0.007448917720466852,0.013792257755994797,0.006840886548161507,0.017937514930963516,-0.0010425497312098742,0.012808999978005886,-0.0066911098547279835,-0.0027564989868551493,-0.004920526407659054,-0.0363072045147419,0.010271926410496235,-0.012295606546103954,0.0001377187727484852,-0.00500780064612627,-0.00983754638582468,0.025364166125655174,0.02965366840362549,-0.028436539694666862,Self-Correction / Feedback Loop,"LLMs, especially when interacting with external tools or performing multi-step reasoning, can make errors (e.g., incorrect tool calls, invalid arguments, logical flaws) that lead to incorrect final answers.","LLM-based agents operate in environments where actions have observable outcomes, and these outcomes can indicate success or failure.","Design the LLM's operational loop to incorporate feedback, either from the environment (e.g., tool execution results, error messages) or through internal self-reflection on its generated thoughts and actions. The LLM then uses this feedback to identify mistakes, revise its plan, or correct its subsequent actions.","Improves the robustness, accuracy, and adaptability of LLM-based systems, allowing them to recover from errors, refine their strategies, and achieve better performance on challenging tasks.","Robust tool-augmented LLMs, complex reasoning agents, interactive systems requiring adaptive behavior.","The Self-Correction / Feedback Loop pattern addresses the common issue of Large Language Models making errors during complex tasks or tool interactions. It works by integrating feedback, either from external environment outcomes or internal self-reflection, into the LLM's operational process. This enables the LLM to identify mistakes, revise its plans, and correct subsequent actions, significantly improving its robustness, accuracy, and adaptability."
