554291725,0.01006318163126707,0.014438624493777752,0.003466374706476927,0.013651619665324688,-0.01484594028443098,0.01553440559655428,0.014269339852035046,0.002949373098090291,0.008708402514457703,-0.01253596507012844,-0.03812835365533829,-0.024170923978090286,0.00019856056314893067,-0.01156998984515667,0.002466854639351368,-0.0019515649182721972,0.012221796438097954,0.023400302976369858,0.032803963869810104,-0.01934857666492462,KNN Exemplar Selection,Selecting effective exemplars for FewShot Prompting can be difficult due to context window limitations and performance dependency on exemplar quality.,When a training dataset (Dtrain) is available and exemplars need to be dynamically selected for a test instance (Dtest_xi).,Select exemplars from Dtrain that are similar to the Dtest_xi using a K-Nearest Neighbor algorithm.,"Boosts performance by providing relevant examples, though it can be time and resource-intensive during prompt generation.",Improving FewShot Prompting performance by selecting relevant examples.,"KNN Exemplar Selection is a Prompt Design pattern that addresses the challenge of dynamically selecting high-quality examples for FewShot Prompting. Specifically, it leverages a K-Nearest Neighbor algorithm to identify and select exemplars from a training dataset that are most similar to the current test instance. While this method significantly boosts performance by providing highly relevant examples, it can introduce time and resource overhead during prompt generation."
