2041283529251814,0.009008217602968216,0.003298472613096237,0.02009967714548111,-0.01978469081223011,0.013620062731206417,0.007254577707499266,0.0067141298204660416,0.007039273623377085,-0.0020252359099686146,-0.023043176159262657,-0.013736306689679623,0.009333685971796513,-0.029006874188780785,-0.006406016647815704,0.0019352918025106192,0.005512719973921776,0.03131388500332832,0.04160694777965546,-0.019233964383602142,MemoryofThought Prompting,Building effective FewShot CoT prompts at test time using unlabeled training exemplars.,"When unlabeled training exemplars are available, and dynamic FewShot CoT prompt construction is desired.","Before test time, perform inference on unlabeled training exemplars with CoT. At test time, retrieve similar instances to the test sample to build FewShot CoT prompts.","Shown substantial improvements in benchmarks like Arithmetic, commonsense, and factual reasoning.","Dynamic FewShot CoT prompt construction, leveraging unlabeled data for reasoning.","MemoryofThought Prompting is an AI pattern designed to dynamically construct effective FewShot Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompts, particularly when unlabeled training exemplars are available. It operates by pre-computing CoT inference on this unlabeled data, then at test time, retrieving similar, pre-processed instances to build context-rich prompts for new queries. This method has shown substantial improvements in benchmarks across arithmetic, commonsense, and factual reasoning, effectively combining FewShot CoT with retrieval-augmented techniques."
