782,0.009034658782184124,-0.0009653507149778306,0.020129038020968437,-0.0023025344125926495,0.01827528327703476,0.0008206185302697122,-0.0021500862203538418,0.0033013999927788973,-0.005847534164786339,-0.017994938418269157,-0.02082984708249569,-0.0016859492752701044,-0.012492303736507893,-0.00016454263823106885,0.00512941787019372,0.000543910835403949,0.024597957730293274,0.03514441102743149,-0.018631046637892723,LeasttoMost Prompting,"Solving complex problems by breaking them down into simpler, sequential subproblems.",When a problem is too complex to solve in a single step and can be naturally decomposed.,"Prompt an LLM to first break a given problem into subproblems without solving them. Then, solve them sequentially, appending model responses to the prompt each time until a final result is achieved.","Shown significant improvements in tasks involving symbolic manipulation, compositional generalization, and mathematical reasoning.","Complex problem-solving, mathematical reasoning, symbolic tasks.","LeasttoMost Prompting is an AI pattern designed to solve complex problems by breaking them down into a sequence of simpler, manageable subproblems. It instructs a Large Language Model (LLM) to first identify these subproblems without solving them, and then to solve each one sequentially, appending previous model responses to the prompt for subsequent steps. This iterative approach significantly improves performance in tasks requiring symbolic manipulation, compositional generalization, and mathematical reasoning."
