0.01796487718820572,-0.0006451993249356747,0.018720008432865143,-0.0033075863029807806,0.011662743985652924,-0.0002603110042400658,0.0009732430335134268,7.835249562049285e-05,-0.002455241745337844,-0.016142509877681732,-0.010723489336669445,0.004396564792841673,-0.009497764520347118,-0.008480093441903591,-0.0008367758127860725,-0.0011173287639394403,0.022368133068084717,0.027503665536642075,-0.019061177968978882,RecursionofThought,"Solving complicated subproblems within a reasoning chain, especially those that might exceed context length.","When an LLM encounters a complex subproblem during its reasoning process that requires deeper, recursive processing.","Every time a complicated problem is encountered in the middle of its reasoning chain, send this subproblem into another prompt/LLM call. After it's completed, the answer is inserted into the original prompt.","Can recursively solve complex problems, including ones which might otherwise run over the maximum context length, showing improvements on arithmetic and algorithmic tasks.","Solving nested complex problems, handling long context reasoning.","RecursionofThought is an AI pattern designed to solve complex subproblems that arise within an LLM's reasoning chain, especially those that might exceed its context length. It operates by recursively sending each complicated subproblem into a new, separate LLM call for independent processing. Once completed, the answer from this sub-call is then inserted back into the original prompt, allowing the model to effectively tackle deeply nested and extensive problems."
