63541007,0.005141399335116148,-0.0017344719963148236,0.024923626333475113,0.0014147883048281074,0.01687081903219223,0.0015794459031894803,0.0016638023080304265,-0.002615752164274454,-0.0019639316014945507,-0.019180091097950935,-0.008828635327517986,-0.0024911921937018633,-0.015513588674366474,0.012546381913125515,-0.0012268880382180214,0.0059196180664002895,0.02856699749827385,0.03658466786146164,-0.021957267075777054,ProgramofThoughts,Improving mathematical and programming-related tasks by leveraging code as reasoning steps.,When tasks involve numerical computation or logical programming constructs.,Use LLMs (like Codex) to generate programming code as reasoning steps. A code interpreter executes these steps to obtain the final answer.,"Excels in mathematical and programming-related tasks, though less effective for semantic reasoning.","Mathematical problem-solving, code generation, algorithmic tasks.","The ProgramofThoughts pattern leverages Large Language Models to generate programming code, which serves as explicit reasoning steps for complex problems. This generated code is then executed by a code interpreter to derive the final answer. It excels in tasks requiring numerical computation, algorithmic logic, and mathematical problem-solving, though it is less effective for purely semantic reasoning."
