920002728700638,0.009325719438493252,0.006787716411054134,0.011257350444793701,-0.019183693453669548,0.009166079573333263,0.012814873829483986,-0.001491588307544589,0.0037633434403687716,-0.00544881634414196,-0.030704021453857422,-0.025673121213912964,0.012566334567964077,-0.01795697771012783,-0.005490937735885382,-0.0008348779520019889,-0.006378465332090855,0.03280948847532272,0.0322008915245533,-0.022656703367829323,Demonstration Ensembling (DENSE),Reducing variance and improving accuracy of LLM outputs in FewShot Prompting.,"When a training set is available, and robustness of FewShot Prompting is desired.","Create multiple fewshot prompts, each containing a distinct subset of exemplars from the training set. Aggregate their outputs to generate a final response.","Reduces the variance of LLM outputs and often improves accuracy, at the cost of increasing model calls.",Improving robustness and accuracy of FewShot models.,"Demonstration Ensembling (DENSE) is an AI pattern aimed at reducing variance and improving the accuracy of Large Language Model (LLM) outputs in FewShot Prompting. It works by creating multiple distinct few-shot prompts, each with a unique subset of exemplars from a training set, and then aggregating their individual outputs. This method enhances the robustness and accuracy of FewShot models, albeit at the cost of increasing the number of model calls."
