26453638,0.0073564667254686356,0.004605788271874189,0.0041344063356518745,0.012322387658059597,-0.011018720455467701,0.015524373389780521,-0.0010387612273916602,-0.002614755416288972,0.011681250296533108,-0.013956869021058083,-0.024178359657526016,-0.02119196578860283,0.008568786084651947,-0.020886385813355446,-0.0016090084100142121,-0.010182657279074192,-0.020706528797745705,0.03533034399151802,0.016378488391637802,-0.025142934173345566,Max Mutual Information Method,Selecting the optimal prompt template from multiple variations.,When multiple prompt templates with varied styles and exemplars have been created.,Select the optimal template as the one that maximizes mutual information between the prompt and the LLM's outputs.,Identifies the most effective prompt template for a given task.,"Prompt optimization, A/B testing of prompt variations.","The Max Mutual Information Method is an AI pattern designed to select the optimal prompt template from multiple variations. It achieves this by identifying the template that maximizes the mutual information between the prompt and the Large Language Model's generated outputs. This process effectively pinpoints the most effective prompt for a given task, significantly aiding in prompt optimization and A/B testing."
