3316436260939,0.005561033729463816,-0.008578640408813953,0.014716860838234425,-0.01613990217447281,0.010048404335975647,-0.0014358451589941978,0.006109151057898998,-0.0026287997607141733,-0.01064301934093237,-0.03254297748208046,-0.01703420653939247,0.0043326374143362045,-0.01911763846874237,-0.008511644788086414,0.007997670210897923,-0.004386551678180695,0.025113392621278763,0.0383475199341774,-0.02383006550371647,MetaReasoning over Multiple CoTs,"Generating a final answer from multiple reasoning chains, even if they don't produce final answers directly.","When multiple CoT reasoning chains are generated, and a consolidated, final answer is needed.","First generate multiple reasoning chains (not necessarily final answers) for a given problem. Next, insert all of these chains into a single prompt template, then generate a final answer from them.","Consolidates diverse reasoning paths into a single, refined answer.","Refining answers from multiple reasoning attempts, complex problem-solving.","The ""MetaReasoning over Multiple CoTs"" pattern addresses the challenge of synthesizing a single, consolidated final answer from several distinct reasoning chains, particularly when individual chains might not directly provide a definitive solution. It operates by first generating multiple Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning paths, then integrating all these diverse chains into a single prompt template to facilitate the generation of the ultimate answer. This method effectively consolidates various reasoning attempts and perspectives, resulting in a more refined and robust final output."
