8,-0.011341078206896782,0.009330433793365955,0.0034797480329871178,0.00772298825904727,0.0138203464448452,-0.006893668789416552,0.010221096687018871,0.0022684219293296337,0.0038058252539485693,0.0060378811322152615,-0.010491644963622093,-0.03620672598481178,-0.016083747148513794,0.004590609110891819,-0.015491013415157795,-0.005743188783526421,-0.008108518086373806,-0.007473744451999664,0.028191542252898216,0.04191255941987038,-0.018993427976965904,Universal Self-Adaptive Prompting (USP),"Generalizing self-adaptive prompting to all tasks, especially using unlabeled data.",When COSP needs to be applied more broadly and leverage unlabeled data for exemplar generation.,"Builds upon COSP, using unlabeled data to generate exemplars and a more complicated scoring function to select them. It does not necessarily use SelfConsistency in the final step.",Aims to make self-adaptive prompting generalizable to all tasks.,"Broadly applicable automated prompt construction, leveraging unlabeled data.","Universal Self-Adaptive Prompting (USP) is an AI pattern designed to generalize self-adaptive prompting across all tasks, particularly by effectively leveraging unlabeled data. It builds upon Consistency-based Self-adaptive Prompting (COSP) by generating exemplars from unlabeled data and selecting them using a more complex scoring function, without necessarily relying on SelfConsistency in the final step. This prompt design technique aims to enable broadly applicable automated prompt construction, making self-adaptive prompting more versatile and efficient."
