4339950624853373,0.012298274785280228,-0.005846780724823475,0.01395008247345686,-0.0074331993237137794,0.019539812579751015,0.009934267960488796,-0.005098415073007345,0.004350294359028339,-0.004873060621321201,-0.009991534054279327,-0.023634031414985657,0.002523557050153613,-0.021010668948292732,-0.004295338410884142,-0.006589667405933142,0.004293684847652912,0.027752893045544624,0.023032967001199722,-0.03026486746966839,ChainofVerification (COVE),Reducing hallucination in large language models by verifying answers with related questions.,"When an LLM generates an answer, and its correctness needs to be verified to reduce hallucinations.","First, use an LLM to generate an answer to a given question. Then, create a list of related questions that would help verify the correctness of the answer. Each question is answered by the LLM, then all the information is given to the LLM to produce the final revised answer.",Shown improvements in various question-answering and text-generation tasks by reducing hallucination.,"Reducing hallucinations, improving factual accuracy in Q&A and text generation.","ChainofVerification (COVE) is an AI pattern designed to reduce hallucinations and improve factual accuracy in large language models. It operates by first generating an initial answer, then prompting the LLM to create and answer a series of related questions to verify the original response. Finally, the LLM synthesizes all this information to produce a more reliable and revised final answer, demonstrating improved performance in various question-answering and text-generation tasks."
