59190166,0.013293248601257801,0.01373656839132309,0.006678890436887741,0.02876860834658146,-0.004676002077758312,0.012080186977982521,-0.001441950211301446,0.0009052633540704846,0.006423537619411945,0.0016133685130625963,-0.01232534646987915,-0.011084765195846558,0.012356214225292206,-0.005700336769223213,0.0012991419062018394,-0.0123238330706954,-0.008613183163106441,0.027997050434350967,0.0375029556453228,-0.021723156794905663,Role-based Evaluation,Improving and diversifying LLM-based evaluations.,When using LLMs as evaluators and needing to generate diverse or specific perspectives on text quality.,"Create prompts with the same instructions for evaluation but different roles (e.g., 'act as a literary critic'). This can also be used in a multi-agent setting where LLMs debate the validity of text.",Effectively generates diverse evaluations and can improve evaluation quality.,"LLM evaluation, quality assessment, multi-agent debate.","Role-based Evaluation is an AI pattern aimed at improving and diversifying LLM-based evaluations by generating specific perspectives on text quality. It works by providing LLMs with evaluation instructions while assigning them distinct roles, such as a literary critic, or by having multiple LLMs debate from different viewpoints. This approach effectively yields diverse and higher-quality assessments, useful for various quality assessment and multi-agent applications."
