9808362722,0.014708434231579304,0.005454429425299168,-0.0028056937735527754,0.004976985510438681,-0.013182033784687519,0.005280393175780773,0.007718656212091446,0.0072148460894823074,-0.010958320461213589,0.0058864401653409,-0.014270881190896034,-0.03483518585562706,0.002015693811699748,-0.0175949577242136,-0.0013579413061961532,0.0013305972097441554,0.0016169791342690587,0.01796397939324379,0.03286634013056755,-0.017738843336701393,Verbalized Score (for confidence calibration),Eliciting confidence scores from LLMs to gauge their certainty.,"When needing to understand the LLM's confidence in its answer, especially when overconfidence is a concern.","A simple calibration technique that generates a confidence score (e.g., 'How confident are you from 1 to 10?') directly in the prompt.","Aims to provide a score representing the model's confidence, though its efficacy is debated.","Assessing LLM confidence, informing user reliance on model outputs.","The ""Verbalized Score"" pattern addresses the challenge of understanding an LLM's confidence in its answers, particularly when overconfidence is a concern. It works by directly prompting the LLM to generate a numerical confidence score, for example, asking ""How confident are you from 1 to 10?"". This aims to provide a quantifiable measure of the model's certainty to inform user reliance, though the efficacy of this self-reported score for true calibration is debated."
