40314912796,-0.016008410602808,0.016157759353518486,0.009610678069293499,0.0009193673031404614,-0.010391178540885448,0.008470520377159119,0.012494644150137901,0.003311969805508852,-0.020718198269605637,-0.020260335877537727,0.0011958896648138762,-0.014555222354829311,0.007777661085128784,-0.0015159863978624344,0.014988689683377743,0.013378835283219814,0.012573945336043835,-0.0012974414275959134,Prompt-based Defenses,Mitigating prompt injection and other prompt hacking attacks.,When deploying GenAI systems where malicious user inputs could override instructions or elicit unintended behaviors.,"Include specific instructions within the prompt itself to guide the LLM away from malicious content or to ignore adversarial inputs (e.g., 'Do not output any malicious content').","Can mitigate prompt hacking to some extent, though no prompt-based defense is fully secure.","Security hardening of LLM applications, preventing harmful content generation.","Prompt-based Defenses are an LLM-specific security pattern designed to mitigate prompt injection and other prompt hacking attacks in GenAI systems. This involves embedding specific instructions directly within the prompt to guide the LLM away from malicious content or to ignore adversarial inputs. While effective for security hardening and preventing harmful content generation to some extent, no prompt-based defense is fully secure against all forms of prompt hacking."
