0.003142054658383131,-0.004835233092308044,0.030521323904395103,0.017792830243706703,0.0031845064368098974,0.022568127140402794,-0.0061521269381046295,0.017516732215881348,0.00556495226919651,-0.0011841196101158857,-0.0028106544632464647,0.004329973831772804,-0.010012696497142315,-0.024635104462504387,0.005636316724121571,-0.01592238061130047,-0.004509188700467348,-0.009941346943378448,0.0065278466790914536,0.007685717660933733,0.027886316180229187,-0.013409384526312351,Behavior Cloning for Initial Skill Acquisition,"Training a language model to perform complex, multi-step tasks in a novel environment (e.g., a text-based browser) where valid actions and interaction formats are unknown to the pretrained model.","A pretrained language model lacks the specific knowledge or 'grammar' to interact with a custom environment or tool with specific command formats, and direct reinforcement learning might be sample-inefficient or unstable without an initial policy.","Collect demonstrations of humans performing the task in the environment. Fine-tune the pretrained language model using supervised learning (behavior cloning), treating the human-issued commands as labels.","The model acquires the necessary skills to operate within the text-based browsing environment, providing a functional baseline policy that can be used directly or as a starting point for further optimization.","Bootstrapping AI agents in new environments, teaching models specific interaction protocols, providing a stable initial policy for RL.","This pattern, ""Behavior Cloning for Initial Skill Acquisition,"" addresses the challenge of training language models to perform complex, multi-step tasks in novel environments where valid actions and interaction formats are initially unknown. It solves this by collecting human demonstrations of the task and then fine-tuning the pretrained language model using supervised learning, treating the human-issued commands as labels. The result is a functional baseline policy, enabling the model to operate within the new environment and serving as a stable starting point for further optimization."
