81343889236,0.0229912381619215,0.02128627337515354,0.022564543411135674,-0.00672227144241333,-0.028574131429195404,0.005047489423304796,0.004041474312543869,0.00949839223176241,0.011124515905976295,-0.014142041094601154,-0.017218193039298058,-0.025171173736453056,-0.0017913385527208447,-0.032389745116233826,0.01393765490502119,-0.0010771702509373426,0.010576634667813778,0.015895763412117958,0.02831795997917652,-0.02333715371787548,Thorough Decoding (RAGSequence),"Accurately approximating arg max_y p(y|x) for the RAGSequence model, where the likelihood p(y|x) does not break into a conventional per-token likelihood, making standard beam search insufficient.","Decoding for the RAGSequence model, which marginalizes over a single latent document for the entire output sequence, requiring a more complex approach than standard autoregressive decoding.","Run beam search independently for each of the top-K retrieved documents. This yields a set of candidate hypotheses. For any hypothesis y that did not appear in the beam of all documents, run an additional forward pass for each document z for which y was not generated. Then, multiply the generator probability p(y|x, z) with the retriever probability p(z|x) and sum these probabilities across all documents to estimate the marginal probability p(y|x).","Provides a more accurate estimation of the marginal likelihood for RAGSequence, leading to potentially better decoding quality, but at the cost of higher computational expense due to multiple forward passes.",High-quality decoding for RAGSequence models when computational resources allow.,"Thorough Decoding (RAGSequence) addresses the challenge of accurately decoding RAGSequence models, where the output likelihood depends on marginalizing over a latent document, making standard per-token beam search insufficient. It achieves this by running independent beam searches for each top-K retrieved document, then re-evaluating candidate hypotheses by calculating their marginal probability across *all* relevant documents. This method provides a more accurate estimation of the marginal likelihood for improved decoding quality, albeit at the cost of significantly higher computational expense due to multiple forward passes."
